@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Active car in the profile button (2026-10-25)
+
+PCA01: Replace the top-menu person icon with the selected car in the Rivalry podium style. PCA02: Follow confirmed car selection and saved paint/parts while preserving profile navigation. R01/Q01: Capture native views, run existing app checks and retain a task-only checkpoint.
+
+`game/ui/profile_car.gd` wraps the existing Rivalry car renderer with the same simple model, front-facing perspective, Garage lighting, paint finish, transparent composite and complete-car framing. It displays a static 72 by 48 logical-unit preview, rendering at twice the display size like the podium. Saved appearance changes and car confirmation refresh it; unchanged appearance keeps the same render. The preview ignores pointer input so the entire profile button remains tappable.
+
+`game/core/app.gd` reserves space for the car in every button state and refreshes it after car selection and Garage synchronization. The name, chevron, profile destination and selection behavior remain intact. Existing models, Rivalry rendering, vehicle configuration and physics are reused without edits. Concurrent changes in the working tree are preserved; the runner's generated build identity is excluded from this task's patch.
+
+Native Compatibility and desktop Mobile reviews rendered all seven selected cars with visible pixels, applied a saved red paint/hood/aero change, retained an unchanged render and opened Profile through an actual touch on the car. Screenshots cover 960×540, 1280×720 and 1720×900 windows. Both renderer reports record successful appearance refresh, retained rendering and profile navigation. Existing `TestApp` passed **141 checks, zero failures**. The new component's check-only parse and the final project import passed. Import retained the environment's nonfatal missing Android build-tools notice.
+
+Commands used the pinned Godot 4.7.2 runner. `APPDATA` and `LOCALAPPDATA` were redirected to `build/profile-car-appdata` for disposable local data. Native runs used reviewed Windows certificate-store access:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action CheckScript -ScriptPath res://ui/profile_car.gd
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestApp -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_profile_car.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod gl_compatibility -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_profile_car.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Import -CommandTimeoutSeconds 180
+```
+
+The Compatibility command also ran once with `BMT_PROFILE_CAR_BASELINE=1`, loading the exact task-start App source only in that isolated process's memory. Initial attempts encountered PowerShell execution policy, a collision between two runner build-identity writes, sandbox log-directory restrictions and certificate-store access restrictions. Sequential runner execution, process-local execution-policy bypass, disposable data directories and reviewed native execution resolved these without changing assertions or production behavior.
+
+Review [before](evidence/profile-active-car-2026-10-25/gl_compatibility/before-compact.png), [after](evidence/profile-active-car-2026-10-25/gl_compatibility/active-compact.png), [customised car](evidence/profile-active-car-2026-10-25/gl_compatibility/customised-compact.png), [forklift](evidence/profile-active-car-2026-10-25/gl_compatibility/active-forklift.png) and [profile opened by tapping the car](evidence/profile-active-car-2026-10-25/gl_compatibility/profile-opened-from-car.png). Both renderer directories contain all-car screenshots and measurement reports. `report.json` records source hashes and checks; `task-only.patch` is checked against the current files in reverse and against task-start files forward.
+
+Client reload and owner/device visual and frame-pacing acceptance remain. No device attachment check or physical-device test, APK, live mutation, purchase, deployment or owner-process restart was performed.
